B.a1C=new A.bX("rop_mcq_4","Before ROP screening, feeds should generally be withheld for:",B.aaF,1,"Before ROP screening, feeds should generally be withheld for 1 hour to prevent regurgitation and aspiration during eye examination.","Preparation Before Screening",null,null)
B.a98=s(["<30 wks gestation and/or <1500g birth weight","<32 wks gestation and/or <1500g birth weight","<34 wks gestation and/or <2000g birth weight","<34 wks gestation and/or <1500g birth weight"],t.s)
B.a1i=new A.bX("rop_mcq_5","Which babies should be screened for ROP based on gestation age and birth weight criteria in India?",B.a98,2,"In India, preterm infants born at <34 weeks gestation and/or <2000g birth weight (or larger preterm infants with an unstable clinical course) should be screened for ROP per national STW guidelines.","Eligibility Criteria",null,null)
B.a7l=s(["2\u20133 weeks after birth","4 weeks after birth","6 weeks after birth","At birth"],t.s)
B.a2_=new A.bX("rop_mcq_6","When should the first ROP screening be done for a baby born at 27 weeks gestation age and 1100g birth weight?",B.a7l,0,"For extremely preterm infants born at <28 weeks gestation, the first ROP screening should be performed earlier, at 2\u20133 weeks after birth.","Timing of First Screening",null,null)
B.a9A=s(["Non-dilating pupil is a good sign.","ROP in Zone I requires Anti-VEGF therapy.","ROP treatments can be safely performed 1 week after diagnosis.","Anti-VEGF treated eyes have low risk of disease reactivation."],t.s)
B.a1d=new A.bX("rop_mcq_7","Which of the following statements is TRUE regarding ROP treatment?",B.a9A,1,"ROP in Zone I (especially Aggressive ROP) is preferentially treated with intravitreal Anti-VEGF therapy. Treatment must be performed within 48\u201372 hours of diagnosis (not delayed by 1 week), non-dilating pupil indicates iris engorgement/rigidity (poor sign/plus disease sign), and anti-VEGF treated eyes have a significant risk of late reactivation requiring prolonged surveillance.","ROP Treatment",null,null)
B.abs=s(["Observe and repeat examination after 2 weeks","Observe and repeat examination after 4 days","Observe, monitor weight gain, encourage KMC, breastfeeding and repeat examination after 2 weeks","Treat with laser photocoagulation within 48\u201372 hours"],t.s)
B.a1z=new A.bX("rop_mcq_8","A 28 weeks 950 g infant undergoes ROP screening and is diagnosed with Zone II stage 1 ROP without plus. What is the most appropriate management?",B.abs,2,"Zone II Stage 1 ROP without plus disease is immature, early disease that does not require immediate intervention. The infant should be observed, weight gain monitored, KMC and breastfeeding encouraged, with repeat examination after 2 weeks.","Management of Stage 1 ROP",null,null)
